---
description: Default new and rebuilt pages to server-side data and HTML; minimize client-only fetching for public content
alwaysApply: true
---

# Server-first rendering (Next.js App Router)

Assume **no one will repeat “make this SSR.”** Implement it by default.

## Public pages (marketing, blogs, news, careers, FAQs, labs, etc.)

- **Fetch CMS and public data on the server** using `tryCreateServerSupabaseClient()` or `createServerSupabaseClient()` from `@/integrations/supabase/server` in `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` (with `Suspense` if needed), or dedicated async Server Components. Prefer **`tryCreateServerSupabaseClient()`** when the UI should still render without env (local preview); use **`createServerSupabaseClient()`** only when missing config must hard-fail.
- **Do not** use `@/integrations/supabase/client`, `useQuery`, or client-side `fetch` for **initial, SEO-relevant content** (titles, body copy, lists, links that crawlers should see).
- Prefer **`export const revalidate = <seconds>`** or **`export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"`** when content must stay fresh; choose based on how often data changes.
- Keep **`"use client"`** only for real browser needs: dialogs, HubSpot/forms, complex client-only interactions, or small wrappers around server-passed props.

## When rebuilding existing pages

- Move **client-side data loading** for public content to the **server** the same way (server fetch → pass serializable props to a thin client component if interactivity is required).

## Exceptions (client-heavy is OK)

- **`/admin`**, **`/auth`**, and similar: auth, mutations, and rich editors may stay client-oriented; still prefer server for **read** of public-facing previews if any.

## Quick pattern

```tsx
// page.tsx — Server Component
const supabase = tryCreateServerSupabaseClient();
if (!supabase) return <YourSection items={[]} />;
const { data } = await supabase.from("…").select("…");
return <YourSection items={data ?? []} />;
```

```tsx
// Only if you need hooks/dialogs: thin client leaf, data from props (already loaded on server).
"use client";
export function YourSection({ items }: { items: Item[] }) { … }
```
